BUILD_ONLY: ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:maniguard-<images/maniguard/VERSION> is never pushed to a public registry
(docs/protocol/README.md §2.4, D5). Every ManiGuard task builds it itself, as its `maniguard-base` stage (this Dockerfile without
its header, copied into the task's environment/Dockerfile and tests/Dockerfile): Harbor builds it on a machine's first
ManiGuard run from public sources only, and every later task reuses the layers. The organization keeps a prebuilt copy in
its private package efe-private, pushed with inline cache metadata; the tasks name it as compose `cache_from`, so a
runner that can read it pulls the layers instead of building them, and one that cannot gets a warning and builds.

Why
  The image contains NVIDIA Isaac Sim 4.5.0.0 / Omniverse Kit (NVIDIA's pip wheels from pypi.nvidia.com), licensed for use,
  not for redistribution, so the built image may not be published. It also contains Spot (GPL-3.0-or-later, conda-forge),
  which is fine in an image that is never distributed.

What the builder accepts (decided by the user before a first build)
  - the NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Omniverse license agreement (the image sets OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=YES and ACCEPT_EULA=Y, and every
    container that runs it accepts it again at launch), as BEHAVIOR-1K's setup.sh --accept-nvidia-eula does;
  - NVIDIA's terms for the Isaac Sim wheels on pypi.nvidia.com;
  - the licences of BEHAVIOR-1K's code (MIT), ManiGuard's code (Apache-2.0), Spot (GPL-3.0-or-later), PyTorch (BSD) and the
    pip / conda-forge packages they pull in.
  No account, key or token is needed for the build: everything is downloaded anonymously. Miniforge uses conda-forge only,
  so no Anaconda terms of service apply (setup.sh's --accept-conda-tos is not needed).

Data (never in the image): $RCB_MANIGUARD_DATA, a host directory with the BEHAVIOR-1K 3.7.2 data root, mounted read-only at
/data by every task (images/maniguard/prep_data.py builds it, tasks/maniguard/README.md):
  behavior-1k-assets/        behavior-1k-assets-3.7.2rc1 (BEHAVIOR Data Bundle: the full set, or the members the
                             selected ManiGuard tasks load; no redistribution)
  omnigibson-robot-assets/   the robot assets BEHAVIOR-1K 3.7.2 downloads (omnigibson-robot-assets.zip, 2025-09-02), plus
                             ManiGuard's long-finger Franka at models/franka/franka_panda_longfinger/ (Apache-2.0)
  omnigibson.key             the BEHAVIOR Data Bundle key (installed after accepting its licence; never copied anywhere)

Host
  Linux x86_64, Docker with BuildKit and the NVIDIA Container Toolkit, an RTX-class NVIDIA GPU. ManiGuard verified driver
  580.x and reports repeatable Isaac Sim 4.5 startup segfaults with newer drivers. Blackwell GPUs (RTX 50 / RTX PRO 6000)
  need torch 2.7.0+cu128 instead of 2.6.0+cu124 (ManiGuard's note): not this image; a separate build, checked separately.
  Build: plan for about 50 GB of free disk (the image is 26 GB on disk; on a host with Docker's containerd image store the
  first build of 2026-10-03 took about 40 GB of the disk in all, with the compressed layers and BuildKit's cache), network
  access to github.com, raw.githubusercontent.com, pypi.org, download.pytorch.org, pypi.nvidia.com, conda.anaconda.org,
  snapshot.ubuntu.com and d4i3qtqj3r0z5.cloudfront.net (NVIDIA's Kit extension CDN); about 5 min alone on an RTX 4090 host
  with a fast link, 19 min as a task's first build on a clean daemon beside other builds (2026-10-19). Running needs no network: the image
  holds every Kit extension the launch resolves (a standard-mode sidecar runs behind the agent's egress allowlist). Run: one Isaac simulator per 32 GB of host RAM. Tested on an RTX 4090 Laptop GPU (16 GB), driver
  580.178.04: a replay peaks at about 4 GB of VRAM.

Build (alone; Harbor does this inside every task's build)
  docker build --target maniguard-base -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:maniguard-$(cat images/maniguard/VERSION) images/maniguard

Check a build (README.md here): the evaluator imports (the build does it), the locks match (the build does it), and a frozen
instance loads to its recorded state hash with the long-finger robot.

Publishing the cache copy (maintainers, after a change here and a VERSION bump)
  Build it as above with --build-arg BUILDKIT_INLINE_CACHE=1, check it (above), push it to
  ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:maniguard-$(cat images/maniguard/VERSION) (organization members only, never a public package),
  and copy the new stage into every task (with the new tag in their compose `cache_from`).
